course: dictionary
lesson: 13689
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «The cricket team's first innings lasted all afternoon.» Here innings means a team's turn to bat in cricket. Ask yourself: does a turn to bat fit the sentence? It does, so that is the meaning.
explain: «Grandma had a good innings, and she lived to ninety-five.» Innings does not mean a turn to bat here. A good innings is a friendly, informal phrase for a long life, and that fits the ninety-five years.
explain: Baseball uses the word too. «In baseball, an inning is one part of the game, and both teams bat once in it.» Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Innings is a noun. In baseball, the singular is inning and the plural is innings.
fact: «Innings» means a team's turn to bat in cricket, or one player's turn at batting.
fact: In baseball, an inning is one of the nine parts of the game, and both teams bat once in each part.
fact: «A good innings» means a long life, and it is informal, mostly used in the UK and Australia.
fact: Clue words like «bat», «runs» and «team» near innings tell you it is about a sport.
exercise: «The cricket team's first innings lasted all afternoon.» What does innings mean here? | A long, happy life | A shop that sells cricket bats | One of nine parts of a baseball game | *A team's turn to bat
exercise: «Grandma had a good innings.» What does this phrase suggest? | She played cricket very well | She won a baseball game | She ran very fast | *She lived a long life
exercise: «In baseball, an inning is one part of the game, and both teams bat once in it.» How many parts does a baseball game have? | *Nine | Three | Twelve | Six
test: Jake says innings always means a long life. Which sentence shows he is wrong? | «She had a long walk home.» | «Grandad had a good innings.» | «He lived in a big house.» | *«The team scored 50 runs in their first innings.»
test: Which meaning fits «Each side had two innings in the match»? | One of the nine parts of a baseball game | *A turn to bat in cricket | A cricket ball | A long, happy life
exam: Which meaning of innings fits «In baseball, an inning is one part of the game, and both teams bat once in it»? | A turn to bat in cricket | A long life | A cricket bat | *One of the nine parts of a baseball game
